course: dictionary
lesson: 802
title: Beforehand: earlier, to get ready
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Beforehand is an adverb. It means earlier, before something else happens, often to get ready. Its clue is time: one thing is done first, and the main thing comes after it.
explain: «To present to the class, you practise beforehand, speak slowly and loudly, and look at the audience.» Practising comes first, before the presenting. Ask yourself: what happens earlier? Swap in «earlier» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The opposite is afterwards. «Tell an adult beforehand where you are going» means tell them first, before you leave. If you said «tell them afterwards», you would be telling them too late to help.
fact: Beforehand means earlier, before something else happens, often to get ready.
fact: The opposite of beforehand is afterwards.
fact: «Their funny stories are often practised beforehand.» The practice happens first, before the show.
fact: In a science experiment, you make a prediction beforehand and test it afterwards.
exercise: Mum says, «Tell an adult beforehand where you are going.» What does beforehand mean here? | After you have come home | Very loudly | Instead of going at all | *Earlier, before you leave
exercise: Which word means the opposite of beforehand? | Soon | Earlier | Ready | *Afterwards
exercise: «Their funny stories are often practised beforehand.» Find and copy the word that means before something else happens. | *beforehand | later | stories | often
test: In a science experiment, when do you make a prediction? | *Beforehand, before you test | Never | At the end of the day | After the test
test: «Asking what will happen beforehand helps.» Why is asking beforehand helpful? | It makes the funeral finish early | It stops you feeling anything | *It lets you know what will happen first | It means you must talk the whole time
exam: Which sentence uses beforehand to mean earlier, to get ready? | Beforehand the cake was eaten at the end | *We practised our lines beforehand so the show went smoothly | The show started beforehand, so we cheered | We went home beforehand, after the show
